WEBVTT
Kind: captions
Language: en

00:00:00.000 --> 00:00:16.280
[Music]

00:00:17.160 --> 00:00:19.000
[Narrator:] This woman is space spraying.

00:00:19.880 --> 00:00:25.860
She is applying a mist of insecticide that will kill the flies and mosquitoes that it contacts.

00:00:26.060 --> 00:00:31.000
It is immediately effective, but it offers only temporary control.

00:00:31.000 --> 00:00:36.180
Other flies and mosquitoes will enter the house and the operation must be repeated.

00:00:36.940 --> 00:00:41.933
This too is space spraying, but on a larger scale and out of doors.

00:00:41.940 --> 00:00:45.640
Here the insecticide may be applied in either of two forms,

00:00:46.240 --> 00:00:50.560
as a mist of tiny droplets that drift slowly downward,

00:00:50.560 --> 00:00:56.740
or as a fog, a blanketing cloud that swirls through shrubbery and between houses.

00:01:06.600 --> 00:01:09.100
In considering outdoor space spraying,

00:01:09.100 --> 00:01:16.200
it is important to realize that the majority of flies and mosquitoes remain within 25 feet of ground.

00:01:16.200 --> 00:01:23.780
This might be termed the insect zone, and it is this region that must be treated to achieve maximum kill.

00:01:24.560 --> 00:01:28.760
Mist applicators are simple in their principle of operation.

00:01:30.140 --> 00:01:34.640
A fan forces a high velocity blast of air past the nozzles.

00:01:34.640 --> 00:01:38.400
The insecticide is injected into this air blast,

00:01:38.400 --> 00:01:44.060
which breaks the liquid into fine droplets and projects them out as a mist.

00:01:45.660 --> 00:01:52.320
There are several types of mist applicators available, some of which project a fine aerosol spray.

00:01:54.540 --> 00:01:58.960
Most of the larger machines can be rotated in a full circle.

00:02:01.900 --> 00:02:05.400
Also, the nozzle can be directed from side to side.

00:02:06.020 --> 00:02:11.600
Here, mist is being projected directly at fly attractants in an alley.

00:02:15.060 --> 00:02:20.520
Where there are no alleys, the mist is directed in a high arc over the houses,

00:02:21.380 --> 00:02:24.800
to drift slowly down through the insect zone.

00:02:27.600 --> 00:02:33.533
The speed of this downward drift is important, and is governed by the size of the droplets.

00:02:33.540 --> 00:02:37.340
If they are large, the mist will fall too rapidly.

00:02:38.160 --> 00:02:43.160
A fast rate of fall shortens the arc and cuts down on the width of the swath covered.

00:02:44.540 --> 00:02:52.133
Droplets of the proper size will carry farther, producing a wide swath, and will continue to drift downward

00:02:52.140 --> 00:02:55.920
in spite of thermals or rising currents of warm air.

00:02:56.840 --> 00:03:02.760
On mist machines, droplet size is regulated by the velocity of the air blast,

00:03:02.760 --> 00:03:06.420
the choice of nozzles, and the weight of oil used,

00:03:06.540 --> 00:03:14.033
heavier oil producing coarser droplets. With fog, fine droplet size is desirable.

00:03:14.033 --> 00:03:18.566
As with mist machines, several types of fog generators are available,

00:03:18.566 --> 00:03:23.240
most of them operated from trucks, although some types are portable.

00:03:24.300 --> 00:03:28.560
A typical thermal generator will illustrate the principle of operation.

00:03:28.560 --> 00:03:33.960
In this machine, air and gasoline are pumped into a combustion chamber and ignited.

00:03:34.700 --> 00:03:40.200
The expanding hot gases pass through the fog head at terrific velocities.

00:03:40.200 --> 00:03:46.440
The insecticide is introduced into the stream of gas and is atomized into fog.

00:03:49.640 --> 00:03:54.200
Contrary to the application of mist, fog is directed along the ground,

00:03:54.200 --> 00:03:58.320
where it swirls around buildings, blanketing the insect zone.

00:03:59.166 --> 00:04:02.720
Since fog is composed of exceedingly fine droplets,

00:04:02.740 --> 00:04:08.340
it is easily affected by thermals and light breezes which will quickly carry it out of the effective area.

00:04:09.200 --> 00:04:17.460
For this reason, fog should be applied at night or in early morning or evening when the air is quiet.

00:04:18.440 --> 00:04:21.720
To measure the effectiveness of space-spray treatment,

00:04:21.733 --> 00:04:26.599
it is important first to make an appraisal of the fly population by the grill method,

00:04:26.600 --> 00:04:29.940
or of the mosquito population by trapping.

00:04:30.300 --> 00:04:36.040
Continued routine sampling during the spray program will indicate the effectiveness of the treatment.

00:04:36.900 --> 00:04:41.680
For most effective application, the equipment should travel at about five miles per hour,

00:04:41.680 --> 00:04:45.633
and mist directed downwind.

00:04:45.640 --> 00:04:51.700
With proper droplet size this will produce a swath 100 feet or more in width.

00:04:55.040 --> 00:04:58.980
Care must be exercised in treating residential districts.

00:04:58.980 --> 00:05:03.460
Oil mist may burn foliage and spot automobiles.

00:05:03.460 --> 00:05:09.280
Therefore fog is frequently used in neighborhoods having expensive landscaping.

00:05:10.840 --> 00:05:14.580
But remember, fog is quickly carried away by light winds and

00:05:14.580 --> 00:05:18.900
thermals which occur during the warm part of the day.

00:05:29.500 --> 00:05:37.100
For best results, fog should be applied during the still hours of night, evening, or early morning,

00:05:37.100 --> 00:05:43.040
but for photographic purposes we are demonstrating fogging technique by daylight in this film.

00:05:43.780 --> 00:05:48.600
Commonly the city block is considered the unit of urban space spraying;

00:05:48.600 --> 00:05:51.766
however, if costly insecticides must be used

00:05:51.766 --> 00:05:56.500
then treatment of the entire block on a citywide basis becomes too expensive.

00:05:58.620 --> 00:06:03.400
Under these circumstances, spot spraying may be employed.

00:06:03.400 --> 00:06:09.433
After an insect concentration is located, spray is applied to this limited area only,

00:06:09.440 --> 00:06:13.700
whether it be a half-block or a single backyard.

00:06:20.440 --> 00:06:24.800
Mist machines can be used effectively for mosquito larva sightings,

00:06:24.800 --> 00:06:28.733
directing the mist downwind so it will carry a sufficient distance,

00:06:28.740 --> 00:06:33.940
producing a film of larvicidal oil on the water surface.

00:06:35.866 --> 00:06:40.800
Airplane space spraying is frequently employed for wide inaccessible areas,

00:06:40.800 --> 00:06:43.240
although airplane application is very expensive

00:06:43.240 --> 00:06:47.360
and should be done in the early morning or late evening hours.

00:06:54.460 --> 00:06:58.600
Commercial indoor equipment is available for use in restaurants,

00:06:58.600 --> 00:07:03.320
but all food and dishes must be covered before spraying is begun.

00:07:04.700 --> 00:07:08.733
It must be emphasized that space spraying depends on contact,

00:07:08.733 --> 00:07:11.999
and has little or no residual effect.

00:07:12.000 --> 00:07:18.133
Partly this is due to insufficient dosage, as the following demonstration will show.

00:07:18.140 --> 00:07:21.920
Here, mist is being applied at a normal rate.

00:07:21.920 --> 00:07:25.980
The fall of mist is picked up on a plate of glass.

00:07:27.060 --> 00:07:31.900
This operator is applying residual insecticide to another glass plate.

00:07:32.060 --> 00:07:36.500
When both plates dry, a comparison will show the difference:

00:07:36.500 --> 00:07:41.300
the dosage of the mist is entirely inadequate for residual effect.

00:07:44.000 --> 00:07:49.033
Space spraying, then, depends on contact to kill insects.

00:07:49.040 --> 00:07:55.300
The effect is immediate, and it is useful to gain quick relief from flies and mosquitoes.

00:07:55.580 --> 00:08:02.760
Outdoors, effective kill depends on treating the insect zone within 25 feet of the ground.

00:08:03.340 --> 00:08:09.780
This may be accomplished by applying a mist of insecticide that drifts slowly down through the zone,

00:08:09.780 --> 00:08:14.760
or a fog that blankets the zone and lingers close to the ground.

00:08:15.440 --> 00:08:19.733
Space spraying is not a cure-all for fly or mosquito problems.

00:08:19.733 --> 00:08:25.199
It has its use for quick relief, but the results are only temporary,.

00:08:25.200 --> 00:08:30.540
However, used intelligently and in conjunction with good sanitation practices,

00:08:30.540 --> 00:08:34.660
space-spraying is a useful tool in any fly-control program.

00:08:34.660 --> 00:08:40.100
[Music]

